# drivers/NativeMobileDisplay on the host:
#   vsync_phase_test                    VsyncPhase.h (r17-touch) against a model compositor at 60 Hz: r8a's quiet
#                                       windows, periodic and rare stalls, a 20 Hz client, a copying compositor, one too
#                                       slow for any phase
#   switch_interaction_test             SwitchInteraction.h: the presents of a touch interaction window, its line
#   switch_frame_stall_test             SwitchFrameStall.h: the frame ends at which the screen stopped mid-animation
#   switch_frame_info_test              SwitchFrameInfo.h: the frame-info keys, each present's entry decoded as
#                                       IOMobileFramebuffer.framework decodes it, the client and pending-swap tables
#                                       (iOS 17's J120 keys; switch_frame_info_24B119_test: iOS 27's J181 keys)
#   display_probe_test                  DisplaySmmuProbe.h against a model of DC A, its CRC unit and the SMMU: passing
#                                       on a working unit and failing at its own stage, undone, for each fault
#   request_state_test                  NativeLegacyRequest.h: which swaps the legacy backend shows itself, the fill,
#                                       the frame scans and colour counts, IOSurface bounds, the bounded row copy
#   native_legacy_display_source_test   how NativeLegacyDisplay.cpp drives the ring, direct scanout, the vsync phase and
#                                       the probe, and hangs its panic restore on SwitchDiag's hook (the driver itself
#                                       is not built for the host); iOS 17's IOMobileFramebufferLegacy table keeps its
#                                       values
#   display_planes_test                 NativePlanes.h (r18-planes): every swap Core Animation can build from the
#                                       published limits accepted (200000 swaps), the refusals, window B's registers
#                                       against drm/tegra's formulas, the CSC table, the layer roles, PlaneLatch
#                                       against a model of DC A with the ARM copy
#   tegra_display_color_test            TegraDisplayColorMath.h against a model of DC A's CMU: the sRGB tables, bit-exact
#                                       passthrough, and what each IOMobileFramebuffer colour input programs
#   tegra_display_color_sequence_test   TegraDisplayColorSequence.h against a raster model of DC A: no CMU word changes
#                                       under the scan, late filters defer, DC A ends on the last tables
#   display_blend_test                  the blend registers window A and B get while a layer is detached, decoded
#                                       with the gen2 blender's factor fields: the UI premultiplied over the layer over
#                                       black, Core Animation's own composite, within half a step at every 8-bit alpha
#   display_column_scan_test            NativeColumnScan.h: window A's column-scan registers against a fetch model held
#                                       to the landscape UI's hardware rotation; the 4K test surface and the reference
#                                       frame showing the same panel; the run's decisions for a pass and each failure
#   display_plane_fence_test            NativePlaneFence.h: window B never writes a surface the GPU renders before its
#                                       writers' work is done, nor later than the present that orders it, against a
#                                       model of the GPU present
#   display_planes_block_test           NativePlanes.h's window B on a GPU block-linear surface: every byte the window
#                                       fetches from its START, H/V_OFFSET and BLOCK_HEIGHT is the surface pixel's own
#                                       (TegraGM20BLayout.h), inside the bytes mapped for it
#   display_planes_source_test          the driver and XNU follow those rules (validateSwap, the kick, one
#                                       STATE_CONTROL pair, retire at the latch, the panic hook, the published limits,
#                                       backboardd's CA_DISABLE_DETACHED gate), and the plane accessors are TegraVIC's
#
#   bazel test //drivers/NativeMobileDisplay/test:all
